story += [p("Abstract", "ChapterEco"), p("EcoSort AI is a deep-learning project that classifies a waste-item image into one of twelve supported dataset categories and presents the result through a responsive web application. The system combines a MobileNetV2 transfer-learning model with a Flask server and a browser interface that supports both photo upload and camera capture. In camera mode, the user sees a live preview, captures a still, reviews it, and explicitly starts prediction; the app does not continuously classify the video feed.")]
story += [p("The repository dataset contains 15,515 images distributed among battery, biological, brown glass, cardboard, clothes, green glass, metal, paper, plastic, shoes, trash, and white glass. Images are loaded at 224 by 224 pixels and split into training and validation sets using an 80/20 configuration and seed 42. The model starts from ImageNet-pretrained MobileNetV2 weights, uses a task-specific twelve-class softmax head, class-weighted training, augmentation, early stopping, and a fine-tuning stage for the final thirty backbone layers.")]
story += [p("The saved metadata reports 94.68% validation accuracy and 0.172 validation loss. These values describe the selected model on the project's validation split; they are not an independent test result or a guarantee for new user photographs. The project outcome is an end-to-end prototype that connects dataset preparation, model training, server-side inference, image upload, camera capture, and a mobile-installable web experience. Further work should establish data provenance, evaluate a held-out test set, report per-class metrics, and improve low-confidence and multi-object handling.")]
